  "slug": "docking-dynamics-049f",
  "summary": "Fresh preprints and a BioLiP3 update extend structure-derived ligand, pocket and fold representations to fragment hits, DDI ranking, antibody screening and design.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is using protein structure, pocket and ligand information as a basis for downstream prediction or design. Pocket coengagement across 21,945 drug pairs is used to prioritize drug-drug interactions, with top-5% precision above background on DDInter and KEGG sets. FoXSight applies Difference-of-Gaussian filtering to multi-reference subtraction maps to detect recurring ligand density in crystallographic fragment screens. FoldAbS repurposes frozen Protenix folding models as encoders for antibody screening, while PartiDesign proposes unified structure-sequence co-design across proteins, nucleic acids and small molecules. A pooled E. coli assay of 39,000+ proteins supports ESMC-MonoYield and inverse-folding benchmarks. BioLiP3 adds curated affinity data with LLM-enabled literature mining. The items are methodologically varied, and the evidence is mostly preprint-level.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-09"
}
